==Restrictions==
Max # of Deployable Cats: 1

==Battleground==
*1 [[Bore]] spawns as the boss after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*1 [[Cyberhorn]] spawns as the boss after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*1 [[Two Can]] spawns as the boss.
*Infinite [[Assassin Bear]]s spawn after 900 seconds<sup>27,000f</sup>, delay 900 seconds<sup>27,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Notably, at a high enough level, [[Talents|Talented]] [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] can deal huge damage to all of the enemies here. With enough luck (and the Target [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] Talent specifically), its Slow ability can immensely help when it activates, as Can Can Cat outranges the major threats of this level and can attack while they struggle to approach instead of attacking.

For the Two Can, certain Cats such as [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] or [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]] can work at a high enough level. Additionally, [[Cutter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Power Cutter Cat]] can come in to deal a quick hit, especially with the boosted attack power and immunity to [[Wave Attack|waves]] in his [[True Form]]. Additionally, Power Cutter is part of [[Brave Cutter (Combo)|Brave Cutter]] and is also an effective choice against Bore for a huge hit.

The Cyberhorn can be a challenging foe. [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] can deal good damage with a chance to freeze. Depending on how often Seafarer freezes, he should come really close to defeating Cyberhorn if not outright emerging victorious. Additionally, if one is to have [[Miter Saw Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Power Saw Cat]], then he should also be effective at tanking several hits and dealing good damage.

Finally, Bore appears. Start by sending out Power Cutter Cat for a quick hit, then send out Roe Cat to hurt him while taking his hits. While a single Roe Cat may not be able to solo this Bore, depending on level and Weaken frequency, it should stick around long enough for the next Roe Cat to be ready to deploy. Eventually, Bore should go down as well. Alternatively, you can send out a Lv.40 [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] with a few [[Cat Combo]]s to kill the Bore.

